    "12": {
      "annotation": "Cohort-level reduction. Scans a sample of the BAMs and sizes windows per reference sequence from the aligned block length distribution, then tiles only the region reads actually reach. Per reference sequence and not pooled, because amplicons differ in depth and fragment length: one cohort-wide size is set by whichever amplicon is deepest and is then too wide for the shallow ones, which lose their locus entirely.",
      "content_id": "haplotype_define_windows",
